# Findings reviewed and accepted, one fingerprint per line.
#
# This file -- not an [allowlist] block in .gitleaks.toml -- is where gitleaks
# takes fingerprints. `allowlist.fingerprints` is not a field gitleaks parses;
# an earlier attempt to put it there was accepted without complaint (unknown
# TOML keys are discarded silently) and suppressed nothing.
#
# The four-part form `commit:file:rule-id:start-line` is the narrowest exception
# gitleaks offers: it exempts exactly one occurrence in one historical commit,
# not a file, a path glob, or a rule. Matching is exact, so a new occurrence
# anywhere else still fails the scan.
#
# 9fd5da7 added a container smoke test to the Image workflow that passed the
# literal `smoke-test-key` in a `curl -H 'X-API-Key: ...'` header, which the
# curl-auth-header rule matches. It was never a credential: the same literal was
# handed to the throwaway container one line earlier as
# RIF_CONTROL_PLANE_API_KEYS, so it authenticated a container that exists for
# ~40 seconds inside the job that created it.
#
# It is already gone from the branch tip -- e55d60e replaced it with a value
# generated per run via `openssl rand` and masked with ::add-mask::, because a
# checked-in key is indistinguishable from a leaked one to a scanner. This entry
# exists only because gitleaks scans commit history, where the original commit
# still contains it.
